.\" Man page for cfl
.TH CFL 1 "August 2026" "Version 1.1" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
cfl \- dual-pane terminal file manager (ncurses)

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cfl
.RI [ directory ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cfl
.RB ( mcfl
branch) is a dual-pane
.B mmenu
file manager. It always starts in jump-to mode scanning
.B $HOME
only. There is no classic browse mode.
.PP
Tab multi-marks entries. Ctrl+V copies and Ctrl+X moves via
marks → clipboard → destination picker under $HOME.
.B q
is always search text; quit with
.BR Ctrl+Q .

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fBdirectory\fR
Optional path (mostly unused for jump root; scan remains $HOME).

.SH KEY BINDINGS

.SS Navigation
.TP
\fBh\fR
Parent directory.
.TP
\fBj\fR / \fBk\fR
Move selection down / up.
.TP
\fBl\fR / \fBEnter\fR
Enter directory or open file.
.TP
\fBg\fR / \fBG\fR
First / last entry in the directory.
.TP
\fBT\fR / \fBM\fR / \fBB\fR
Top / middle / bottom of the current view.
.TP
\fB.\fR
Toggle hidden files.
.TP
\fBu\fR
Reload current directory.

.SS Search and pickers
.TP
\fB/\fR
Fuzzy search in the current directory (left: matches, right: live preview).
Enter jumps to the match; Esc cancels. Matches prefer shorter names when ranked.
.TP
\fBJ\fR
Jump-to mode: scan directories under
.BR /home ,
.BR /etc ,
and
.B /usr
(errors and basenames in
.B JUMP_OMIT_DIRS
omitted). Type to filter; Enter opens the directory; Esc cancels.
Symlinks are not followed. Results prefer shorter paths.
.TP
\fBD\fR
Remove-search mode: filter the
current directory, Tab multi-marks items (dark red), right panel shows details.
Enter opens a sticky confirm listing every target (all marked rows, or the
focused match). Enter/t moves to FreeDesktop Trash (default); d permanently
deletes; n/Esc cancels.
.TP
\fBm\fR
Move-to mode: with a non-empty selection, pick a destination directory
(same scan as jump-to) and move the selection there. Current browsing
directory is unchanged.
.TP
\fBC\fR
Copy-to mode: like move-to, but copies instead of moving.

.SS File operations
There is no global VISUAL multi-select.
.B Tab
marks items inside tools
.RB ( m , C , D )
or focuses sticky preview panels
.RB ( ? , = , n ).
.TP
\fBm\fR
Move-to: Tab multi-mark sources in the current directory, Enter, then pick a
destination (same scan as jump-to).
.TP
\fBC\fR
Copy-to: like move-to, but copies.
.TP
\fBr\fR
Rename-to mode: filter the current directory (dual-pane, like search),
Enter to pick a file, type the new basename, Enter renames in place.
Esc cancels.
.TP
\fBD\fR
Remove-search (see modes section): Tab multi-mark, Enter/t trash, d permanent.
.TP
\fBn\fR
Create a new empty regular file in the current directory.
Opens a sticky name prompt in the preview panel: type a name, Enter creates,
Esc cancels.
.TP
\fBN\fR
Create a new directory in the current directory (same sticky preview prompt as
.BR n ).
.TP
\fB!\fR
Open a shell in the current directory.

.SS Preview and info
.TP
\fBi\fR
Toggle file-info mode. The right panel shows metadata instead of previews;
Überzug image previews are stopped. Status shows
.BR [INFO] .
Images: resolution and proportion. Videos: resolution, proportion, FPS,
codec, duration, and size (via
.B mediainfo
when available).
.TP
\fBK\fR
Scroll preview pane up.
.TP
\fB[\fR / \fB]\fR
Page up / page down in the preview pane.
.TP
Image previews (Überzugpp) only clear the previous image when the next
image is smaller or not an image; equal or larger images are drawn without
a full clear for faster browsing.

.SS Other
.TP
\fB!\fR
Open a shell in the current directory.
.TP
\fB?\fR
Toggle sticky keybindings help in the preview panel (no modal). The file list
stays fully interactive so you can try the bindings while reading them. Tab
moves focus to the help pane (filter/scroll); Esc on the help pane closes help
and restores the normal preview.
.TP
\fBq\fR
Quit. Writes the last browsed directory to the lastdir file (see
.BR CFL_LASTDIR ).
With
.B /usr/share/cfl/cfl.sh
sourced, the interactive shell then
.B cd
s to that directory.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHELL
Shell for
.BR ! .
Default
.BR /bin/bash .
.TP
.B EDITOR
Editor environment variable. Default
.BR nvim .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Config base (default
.BR $HOME/.config ).
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Data base for Trash (default
.BR $HOME/.local/share ).
.TP
.B CFL_LASTDIR
File path written on quit with the last directory. Default
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cfl/lastdir .

.SH FILES
.TP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cfl/clipboard.<pid>\fR
Session-local transfer list. Not shared across instances; removed on exit and
after consuming file operations.
.TP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cfl/lastdir\fR
Last directory on quit (for shell helper).
.TP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cfl/scripts\fR
Executable external scripts.
.TP
\fB/usr/share/cfl/cfl.sh\fR
Shell function wrapper for
.B cd
on quit (installed with the package).
.TP
\fB$XDG_DATA_HOME/Trash\fR
FreeDesktop home trash:
.B files/
holds items,
.B info/*.trashinfo
holds original path and deletion date. Not a raw
.B mv
dump folder.

.SH CONFIGURATION
Compile-time options live in
.BR config.h
(keys, opener, hidden files, jump omit list, Überzugpp settings, panel
borders). Interactive UI uses sticky preview panels; short messages use the
status line. Rebuild after editing.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B cfl
Open the current directory.
.TP
.B cfl ~/Downloads
Open a specific directory.
.TP
.B source /usr/share/cfl/cfl.sh
Enable quit-into-last-directory, then run
.BR cfl .

